## Negative findings (why this file is `.excluded`)

**ZERO verified public benchmark numbers were found for this exact model/ID.** Per the self-exclusion rule this file is saved as `GLM_5.3.md.excluded` — no scored `.md` is written, and no placeholder scores are invented.

What was verified (2026-10-23, catalog/pricing metadata only, no measured numbers):

- **Identity:** GLM-4.5-Flash — Z.ai's free-tier lightweight model of the GLM-4.5 generation (flagship GLM-4.5 is a 355B MoE; the Flash is its distilled fast sibling), released 2025-07-28 (models.dev `zhipuai/glm-4.5-flash`).
- **Specs (models.dev):** 131,072 context / 98,304 max output; reasoning yes (dual thinking modes per curated meta); tool call yes; open weights; text in/out only.
- **Pricing (official Z.ai pricing docs, fetched 2026-10-23):** GLM-4.5-Flash = **Free / Free / Free / Free** (input / cached input / cache storage / output) on the Z.ai developer platform — the free lane still exists alongside GLM-4.7-Flash (also Free).
- **Zen availability:** the live OpenCode Zen models endpoint (fetched 2026-10-23) does NOT currently serve a `glm-4.5-flash` id (GLM entries: glm-5, glm-5.1, glm-5.2, glm-5.3, glm-5.3-flash, glm-5.3-flash-free) — the curated "Free on Zen" note is stale; free access is via the Z.ai platform today.

Sources checked with no Flash-specific benchmark rows (2026-10-23):

- **BenchLM** (`glm-4-5-flash`): 404 — no page. The GLM-4.5 family page tracks the flagship only (4 rows, unranked: Vals LiveCodeBench 67.4%, GPQA-D 72.2%, MMLU-Pro 81.2%, Design Arena 1171 — all measured on `zai_glm-4.5`, the 355B flagship, NOT the Flash). The BenchLM Z.AI family list includes `glm-4-7-flash` (39.07) and `glm-4-5-air` (34.85) but no `glm-4-5-flash`.
- **Artificial Analysis** (`glm-4-5-flash`): 404 — no page for the Flash variant.
- **models.dev:** specs/pricing only, no benchmark fields.
- **Hugging Face** (`zai-org/GLM-4.5-Flash`): repo fetch gated (401) in this pass — no readable model card.
- **z.ai:** no GLM-4.5-Flash model page (404); the official pricing docs carry no benchmark table.

Flagship interpolation was deliberately NOT used: the GLM-4.5 rows above are measurements of the 355B flagship; the Flash is a smaller distilled model with lower headroom (per the curated meta's own note), so transplanting flagship numbers onto the Flash ID would fabricate evidence — the same pattern already recorded for the sibling `model/glm-4.6-flash/` ("no published Flash-specific benchmarks; Z.ai publishes flagship numbers only").

A future re-research should look for (a) a readable GLM-4.5-Flash model card with its own benchmark table (HF or Z.ai), (b) aggregator coverage (BenchLM/AA) once the variant is measured, (c) any Vals/AA evaluation of the `glm-4.5-flash` id specifically — then write a fresh `GLM_5.3.md`.

Scores inside this file are intentionally omitted/ignored: the sync skips `.excluded` files loudly.

